wlanpi-mcp (0.6.14-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship wlanpi-mcp-ufw-first-boot.service. It was dropped from
    debian/wlanpi-mcp.install in 0.3.4 and never reached the package, so
    the postinst on image builds (chroot) found no unit to enable and
    fresh images booted with 8766/8767 closed until a later wlanpi-mcp
    upgrade ran the UFW setup script. The unit is now installed and
    managed by dh_installsystemd (--no-start), matching wlanpi-core, so
    it is enabled on image builds and apt installs and removed on purge.
    The postinst's hand-rolled systemctl enable is gone. Fixes #33.

