wlanpi-mcp (0.6.12-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace the legacy SSE transport with stateless streamable HTTP on /mcp.
    Claude Code re-opened a dropped SSE stream (daemon restart, idle gap)
    without re-sending initialize, and the MCP SDK then answered every tool
    call on that session with -32602 Invalid request parameters until the
    client was restarted (python-sdk issue #2579, closed as not planned).
    Stateless mode has no server-side session to strand on: every POST /mcp
    is a complete exchange. Responses are plain JSON (json_response), so the
    nginx front needs no long-lived stream and curl debugging is simple.
  * Token passthrough now reads the Bearer off the request the transport binds
    to each MCP call (get_token), with the middleware contextvar as fallback,
    so the token reaching wlanpi-core is always the one on that request.
  * /sse is no longer served. Clients change the path to /mcp and the
    transport to http (Claude Code: --transport http; mcp-remote:
    --transport http-only). nginx site, systemd unit and docs updated.

 -- Jake Snyder <jsnyder81@gmail.com>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:45:00 +0000

wlanpi-mcp (0.6.11-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Verify the capture WebSocket against WLANPI_CORE_CA. connect_capture
    called websockets.connect with no SSL context, so it fell back to the
    system trust store and rejected wlanpi-core's self-signed cert
    (CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED), breaking every capture tool even though the
    REST client verified fine against the same CA.
  * Stop the SSE daemon writing bytecode at runtime (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE).
    Python created __pycache__/*.pyc under the installed package, which dpkg
    does not own, so 'apt purge wlanpi-mcp' left
    /opt/wlanpi-mcp/.../site-packages/wlanpi_mcp behind.

 -- Josh Schmelzle <josh@joshschmelzle.com>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:10:00 -0400

wlanpi-mcp (0.6.10-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix SSE connections through the nginx front failing with 421 Misdirected
    Request. Since the daemon moved to a loopback-only bind (0.6.8), the MCP
    SDK auto-enabled DNS rebinding protection for host=127.0.0.1 and rejected
    the LAN Host header that nginx forwards (proxy_set_header Host $http_host),
    so every GET /sse on 8766/8767 was refused. The server now disables that
    check explicitly: the transport is protected by the mandatory wlanpi-core
    Bearer JWT, which a rebinding page cannot supply. Adds regression tests
    that drive the assembled SSE app with forwarded LAN Host/Origin headers.

 -- Jake Snyder <jsnyder81@gmail.com>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:45:00 -0400

wlanpi-mcp (0.6.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Offer both SSE endpoints behind the nginx front: TLS on 8767 (preferred,
    self-signed cert) and a plaintext fallback on 8766 for MCP harnesses that
    cannot validate the self-signed cert (e.g. goose, which has no way to skip
    cert verification). Both require the wlanpi-core Bearer JWT; on 8766 the
    token crosses the LAN in cleartext, so that port is documented as a
    trusted-network/development fallback and the trust-store path is called
    out for harnesses that can support it.
  * The uvicorn upstream moves from 8767 to 127.0.0.1:8768 so nginx can own
    8767 for TLS. postinst chains the port migrations (8766->8768 and
    8767->8768), UFW now opens 8766/tcp and 8767/tcp, and the install banner
    lists both endpoints.

