wlanpi-mcp (0.6.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: front the SSE daemon with nginx so the wlanpi-core JWT no longer
    crosses the LAN in cleartext. The uvicorn daemon now binds loopback-only
    (WLANPI_MCP_HOST=127.0.0.1, WLANPI_MCP_PORT=8767) and an MCP-owned nginx
    site terminates TLS on 8766 with the device's self-signed cert; clients
    connect to https://<wlanpi>:8766/sse, same port, scheme only. /sse and
    /messages/?session_id=... map 1:1, so no root_path handling is needed. The
    upgrade postinst migrates existing config to the loopback bind and reloads
    nginx; UFW keeps opening 8766/tcp. postrm removes the site conf.
  * Fix stale WLANPI_CORE_URL=http://localhost:31415 in config.env.example
    (the https default was already the code/config default).

