wlanpi-mcp (0.6.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * capture: capture_scan/capture_observe now also save the raw pcapng to the
    managed capture directory (Settings.PCAP_CAPTURE_DIR) while returning the
    dissected summary, and report it as 'pcap_path'/'pcap_bytes'. This lets the
    streaming summary be verified against the frames with fetch_pcap_file. The
    saved file uses the same naming as the file-capture tools, so it is also
    listed by list_pcap_files and fetchable by capture_id. Teeing is
    best-effort, so a storage problem never breaks a capture.
  * capture: factor the capture directory, filename scheme and path-confinement
    check into wlanpi_mcp/capture/storage.py, shared by both the streaming tee
    and the file-capture tools.

