wlanpi-mcp (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * capture: greatly expand the dissector now that only the summary is
    returned. AP rows carry the full 802.11 security picture - the AKM suite
    list, pairwise and group ciphers, and PMF (MFPC/MFPR) - alongside the
    compact security label. A new per-frame log covers every frame type: each
    record names the type/subtype, lists the source/destination addresses
    (addr1..addr4), carries a full radiotap decode, and, for the frames that
    carry one, a decoded result (auth algorithm/status, assoc status/AID,
    deauth/disassoc reason, probe/assoc SSID). Exact per-kind counts are always
    returned; the per-frame record list is capped by max_frames (0 disables it)
    so a busy capture stays a summary. The pcapng reader now yields a per-frame
    timestamp (if_tsresol-aware).

